    "R22 identified the R21 mechanism: lowering isotropic coefficient-prior variance increased posterior expected graph size by 1.31 edges and overestimated true graph size in 12/12 worlds, indicating a marginal-likelihood complexity/Occam-factor distortion rather than simple over-shrinkage.",
